WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club

﻿1

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:00.160
<i>You got a cloudy Monday ahead today
here in the nation's capital.</i>


00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:04.848
<i>Chance of rain showers and a likely
chance of some drizzle that continues...</i>


00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:08.320
<i>With President Nixon
facing an uncertain re-election,</i>


00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.080
<i>candidates for the Democratic Party
are accusing him</i>


00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:14.323
<i>of failing to end
American involvement in Vietnam.</i>


00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:17.487
<i>Members of the Committee
to re-elect the President</i>


00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.920
<i>were in Jacksonville today
on their campaign trip through Florida.</i>


00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.000
<i>And for a report on that,
here's Georgia Wilson.</i>


00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:27.129
<i>Wife of the Attorney General,
Mrs. Richard Kleindienst.</i>


00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:32.529
<i>This is the final weekend
of our month-long extravaganza sale.</i>


00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:35.240
<i>All sizes all on sale!</i>


00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:37.840
<i>In Washington,
yet another public demonstration</i>


00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:40.685
<i>by some citizens opposed to the Vietnam War.</i>


00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.849
<i>Reporter Alan Witten.</i>


00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:45.850
<i>It was festive
as the crowd turned to Capitol Hill.</i>


00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.120
<i>In an hour's time,
several thousand people had joined hands</i>


00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.490
<i>to form a complete circle of war protest
around the US Capitol.</i>


00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:04.320
<i>Clean and Shine to the rescue!
Cleans up stains,</i>


00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:08.440
<i>only the shine remains. No rubbing.
No trimming, no foul smells.</i>


00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.600
<i>A sharp recession
has shaken economic confidence.</i>


00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.880
<i>As a result, a large field of
Democratic challengers has emerged</i>


00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:17.800
<i>and would beat Nixon
if the elections were held today.</i>


00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:20.160
- <i>Five different flavors!</i>
- <i>Five different meals!</i>


00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.322
<i>One happy family!</i>


00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:45.241
<i>One, two, three, four!
We don't want your fucking war!</i>


00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:49.201
<i>One, two, three, four!
We don't want your fucking war!</i>


00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:54.965
<i>Mark Felt.</i>


00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:03.605
Gentlemen. Mr. Dean.


00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:05.928
Goddamn Russian revolution out there.


00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:08.490
Why aren't we arresting anybody?


00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:11.121
Because that isn't a crime.


00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.560
Right now the president needs your advice.


00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:20.520
Yeah, Hoover's run the FBI, what, 40 years?


00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:23.280
- Fifty.
- Fifty goddamn years.


00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:26.603
You know, Johnson and Kennedy
wanted to fire him, don't you?


00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:28.160
But they didn't have the balls.


00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:33.366
If the president were to ask
Mr. Hoover to step aside,


00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:35.924
how would you suggest he do it?


00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:41.400
We know you to be a friend
of this administration.


00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:43.722
We like to see our friends
get what they deserve.


00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:48.523
- You're next in line.
- There is no line, Mr. Mitchell.


00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:50.563
The president is asking.


00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:56.722
Mr. Hoover would want to keep
his bullet-proof car.


00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:02.766
You're a real politician, Felt.


00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.402
Then thanks for popping by.


00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:10.881
If I may.


00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:17.125
There is one thing Mr. Hoover knows
that's been on all your minds.


00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:23.920
Whenever the FBI hears
a piece of gossip or information,


00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:29.166
such as "I saw so-and-so out
with another woman, not his wife,"


00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:32.969
or a man, not his wife,


00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.160
we're supposed
to write everything down, and we do.


00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:38.129
We write it all down in memos.


00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:41.084
These memos come to me,


00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:44.761
and I decide what information
Mr. Hoover needs to know,


00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:47.202
and send that up to Mr. Hoover.


00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:51.048
And Mr. Hoover puts it all away
in his private files,


00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:53.969
to be kept safe,


00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:57.160
out of the hands of people
without discretion,


00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:01.882
people who could do harm should that
information be leaked, for instance,


00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.368
and put before the court of public opinion.


00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:09.920
And then sometimes Mr. Hoover
will go, for instance,


00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.846
to the president's closest aides and say,


00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:17.640
Mr. Ehrlichman or Mr. Mitchell,


00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:20.240
"I want you to know
that we received that report


00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:21.920
"about you and that other woman,


00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:25.971
"and I want to tell you
that there is absolutely no reason


00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:28.880
"for us to take any further action.


00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:31.361
"There is no violation.


00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:34.440
"You're safe.


00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:36.170
"We, the FBI...


00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:40.927
"All your secrets are safe with us."


00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:47.568
How long have you been in the FBI, Felt?


00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:51.522
Thirty years.


00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:55.849
That's a lot of information, a lot of files.


00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:01.921
Thank you, Mr. Felt.


00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:04.891
Thank you, gentlemen. Mr. Dean.


00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:15.723
Choke on your Manhattan.


00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:17.968
Have a little something.


00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:20.560
- Hello, darling.
- Hey, sweetie.


00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:24.964
I give you the chief dragon slayer
and guardian of the American dream.


00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:29.769
Come on, Mark. Crack a smile, at least!


00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:32.080
Eddie, let me go.


00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:34.561
Eddie, leave her alone.
She's the best. Come here, you.


00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:36.040
- Did you hear that?
- I need a drink.


00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:37.167
- I am the best.
- I heard that.


00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:39.607
- Hi, hon.
- Hi, sweetie.


00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:43.000
- Look what I've done.
- Look what you're doing.


00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:44.127
What were you doing?


00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:53.406
Yes, sir.


00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:05.563
Keep the hips down.


00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:09.080
Look at your feet.


00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:11.402
Come on, attitude.


00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:13.568
Eddie, they're elegant!


00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:21.002
- Good morning.
- Good morning.


00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:25.443
- Is the director in?
- Not yet.


00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:34.203
Here's that Weather Underground file.


00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:51.480
- How many bombings now?
- Couple dozen.


00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:53.480
Precise numbers, Mr. Miller.


00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:54.760
Twenty-nine.


00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:56.570
Nails and ball bearings.


00:09:56.680 --> 00:09:58.887
These kids aren't messing around.


00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:03.129
They're embarrassing the FBI.


00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:05.890
Get the New York office.


00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:09.281
He's dead.


00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:11.081
Who?


00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:13.611
Mr. Hoover's dead.


00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:17.922
His housekeeper found him on the floor.


00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:19.840
He wasn't breathing.


00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:21.968
It looks like a stroke.


00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:29.129
Put everything into motion.


00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:33.244
No mistakes, gentlemen. Not one.


00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:20.720
Good morning, Felt.


00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:22.720
The assistant Attorney General.


00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:24.006
Pat Gray.


00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:26.160
Complicated morning for all of us.


00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:29.840
Indeed. Mr. Miller, here, will be
handling the funeral arrangements.


00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:32.600
I have the Attorney General's
instructions on seating and protocol.


00:11:32.680 --> 00:11:34.160
The funeral will be handled by the FBI.


00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:36.640
The Attorney General
will sit beside the vice president.


00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:39.769
Handled by the FBI in its own way, Mr. Gray.


00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:45.164
I also have instructions
on Mr. Hoover's files.


00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:48.329
I am to take possession of them
and bring them to the White House.


00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:50.483
What files?


00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:56.881
Mr. Hoover's secret files.
The Personal and Confidentials.


00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:00.360
Official and Confidentials.


00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:02.443
There are no secret files.


00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:52.531
<i>We thank thee this day
with arms open for J. Edgar Hoover,</i>


00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:55.565
for his lifelong trust in thee,


00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:58.326
his steadfast devotion to the nation,


00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:00.887
his elevated patriotism,


00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:04.881
his commitment to justice
and peace in the nation.


00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:10.160
We ask that we may be as strong,


00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:13.411
- brave as he was brave...
- Excuse me.


00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:16.280
- Loyal as he was loyal...
- Pardon me.


00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:18.442
Serve as he served,


00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:22.566
love the nation as he loved it.


00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:40.160
Felt!


00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:43.524
Jesus. Bill Sullivan.


00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:47.689
I'd like a word with you.


00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:55.720
Bill Sullivan and Mark Felt, together again.


00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:56.960
Who would have thought it?


00:13:57.040 --> 00:13:59.000
I think I was the one
who recommended you to the old man


00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:00.160
for your first big promotion.


00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:03.210
- You know you were.
- That's right. Mark Felt never forgets.


00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:05.165
That's why everyone likes you.


00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:08.240
Hell, I even like you.


00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:09.765
And I don't like anybody.


00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:11.371
What do you want?


00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.242
I had 30 years in the bureau.


00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:17.400
Same as you.


00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:19.480
- You were the director's bag man.
- Yeah?


00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:22.040
You taped Martin Luther King with other women


00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:24.362
and sent the pictures to his wife.


00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:26.923
Do you need me to actually say it?


00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:31.089
Those days were gone. You had to go.


00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:38.567
You could be you, Mark,
only because I was who I was.


00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:42.760
You and I were an ecosystem.


00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:45.047
That's how nature works.


00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:47.163
Keeps everything in a balance.


00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:50.924
Now, the king is dead.


00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:53.130
Long live the king.


00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:57.445
- Are you the new king?
- You tell me.


00:14:57.880 --> 00:15:00.451
You're the president's new best friend.


00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:04.651
Mark Felt.


00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:09.128
Integrity, bravery, fidelity.


00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:11.004
Ladies and gentlemen, the G-man's G-man.


00:15:11.280 --> 00:15:14.363
You want to know what everybody
really thinks of you? Do you?


00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:19.120
Competent, reliable, loyal.


00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:21.282
- What's wrong with that?
- Nothing.


00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:24.408
If you're a golden retriever.


00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:26.961
Hoover's gone.


00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:30.171
You're alone now,


00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:35.808
holding the end of your own leash.


00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:57.204
<i>Attorney general, line one.</i>


00:16:08.600 --> 00:16:09.647
Dick.


00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:14.040
Yes.


00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:17.240
Well, I have enjoyed every day of it.


00:16:17.320 --> 00:16:22.087
The FBI has been home to me
and my family for 30 years and...


00:16:23.240 --> 00:16:24.287
Yes.


00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:34.770
"A new day."


00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:39.045
Yes, a fresh start.


00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:41.766
It's what I would do.


00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:46.203
Who do you have in mind?


00:16:49.240 --> 00:16:52.164
I'm sorry. Could you repeat that? Who?


00:16:57.200 --> 00:17:00.249
- Welcome to the FBI.
- A friendly face.


00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:01.640
Gentlemen.


00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:03.720
Now, Mr. Gray.


00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:06.849
I know the bureau
has its closets and skeletons.


00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.526
You can count on me to keep those doors shut.


00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:11.600
I'll be candid with you.


00:17:11.680 --> 00:17:13.762
I was a submarine commander in the navy.


00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:17.521
I was father, confessor and friend
to 18-year-olds.


00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:19.210
Did you know that?


00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:22.080
I'm not a suspicious man by nature.


00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:24.920
That probably makes me
a strange choice to run the FBI.


00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:27.970
In fact, when the president called my wife


00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:30.048
she begged me to turn him down, but...


00:17:31.920 --> 00:17:34.924
But the president wasn't asking,
if you know what I mean.


00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:40.245
Now, let me be candid with you, Mr. Gray.


00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:44.280
The FBI is the most respected
institution in the world.


00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:47.360
It is one of the two cockpits
that fly America,


00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:52.242
and it is what it is because no one
from the outside ever got inside.


00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:56.080
Mr. Hoover has been old, a long time.


00:17:56.160 --> 00:17:58.080
We all know it's been you running
the FBI, Felt.


00:17:58.160 --> 00:18:00.606
- Your reputation is stellar.
- Let me finish.


00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:04.405
You have no law enforcement experience.
You're an outsider.


00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:08.160
That is your battle to fight,
but I'm going to help you.


00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:10.004
- Well, I appreciate that.
- Don't.


00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:12.527
It's not an act of generosity.


00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:15.720
This is about this building
and what goes on in here


00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:17.689
and what it means to the country.


00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:19.570
That is all I care about.


00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:23.483
As long as you keep the FBI first,


00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:25.643
you'll be able to count on me.


00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:32.851
This is your office.


00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:02.523
I thought the job was yours.


00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:07.530
What did I miss?


00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:17.208
You and Mr. Hoover.


00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:24.610
Don't you remember
why he said he liked you so much?


00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:29.409
He always said
you and he had the same enemies.


00:19:31.840 --> 00:19:33.604
That's why.


00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:41.091
Thirty years.


00:19:44.760 --> 00:19:46.444
Thirteen transfers.


00:19:50.480 --> 00:19:52.084
Thirteen homes to leave.


00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:55.286
Thirteen homes to make.


00:19:56.720 --> 00:19:59.565
I left behind every friend I ever made.


00:20:00.560 --> 00:20:02.840
And I kept my mouth shut,


00:20:02.920 --> 00:20:05.241
like the perfect little FBI wife.


00:20:07.400 --> 00:20:08.840
Until one day you wake up


00:20:08.920 --> 00:20:10.600
and you're so different than you used to be


00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:14.082
you can't even remember
what the point was in the first place.


00:20:15.920 --> 00:20:19.925
Till there's just one thing left in my head.


00:20:20.960 --> 00:20:27.047
The one idea left in my head is,
at least Mark's going to get that job.


00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:29.891
- And that will make up for everything.
- Audrey.


00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:33.248
They don't deserve you.


00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:36.401
They don't deserve us.


00:20:41.080 --> 00:20:42.650
You need to resign.


00:21:07.800 --> 00:21:10.406
When the bureau is in better hands,


00:21:12.800 --> 00:21:14.450
then, I'll go.


00:21:32.360 --> 00:21:34.647
- What is it?
- <i>This is getting complicated.</i>


00:21:34.800 --> 00:21:36.609
<i>You better get down here.</i>


00:21:36.840 --> 00:21:39.920
<i>Five men wearing white gloves
and carrying cameras</i>


00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:41.800
<i>were caught early today in the headquarters</i>


00:21:41.880 --> 00:21:44.680
<i>of the Democratic National Committee,
in Washington.</i>


00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:46.000
<i>They apparently were unarmed</i>


00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:49.323
<i>and nobody knows yet
why they were even there.</i>


00:22:07.520 --> 00:22:08.931
Mr. Kunkel.


00:22:09.760 --> 00:22:12.969
Straight into the Democrat offices
in the Watergate.


00:22:14.360 --> 00:22:16.000
Who's our spy?


00:22:16.080 --> 00:22:17.764
Baldwin, Alfred C.


00:22:17.920 --> 00:22:19.920
Checked in six weeks ago.


00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:21.920
Says he was more than just the lookout.


00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:24.048
He says he was supposed
to listen for "girlie stuff."


00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:26.600
Guess the Dems are having
a lot of trouble with their wives.


00:22:26.680 --> 00:22:28.360
He say where he got his instructions?


00:22:28.440 --> 00:22:30.443
Baldwin is one of ours.


00:22:31.200 --> 00:22:33.123
Ex-FBI.


00:22:33.960 --> 00:22:35.405
He worked under Bill Sullivan.


00:22:36.320 --> 00:22:38.960
When he was in the bureau,
was he in Mr. Sullivan's group?


00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:40.240
We think so.


00:22:40.320 --> 00:22:42.240
What about CIA connections?


00:22:42.320 --> 00:22:43.651
No idea. Why?


00:22:44.200 --> 00:22:47.480
Because 30 minutes ago
four of those burglars told a judge


00:22:47.560 --> 00:22:49.563
they are ex-CIA.


00:22:51.280 --> 00:22:53.123
What the hell is this?


00:22:54.480 --> 00:22:56.880
<i>One of the most fascinating
and exotic stories</i>


00:22:56.960 --> 00:22:58.800
<i>ever to come out of Washington, DC,</i>


00:22:58.880 --> 00:23:00.960
<i>is the talk of the capital today.</i>


00:23:01.040 --> 00:23:03.088
<i>Robert Endicott covered the story.</i>


00:23:03.200 --> 00:23:05.720
<i>Democratic officials today
held a series of meetings</i>


00:23:05.800 --> 00:23:07.400
<i>to talk about tighter security</i>


00:23:07.480 --> 00:23:08.960
<i>at the national headquarters
here in Washington.</i>


00:23:09.040 --> 00:23:11.200
<i>The White House has so far
offered no official comment,</i>


00:23:11.280 --> 00:23:14.880
<i>but a close adviser to the president,
seen here visiting China last month,</i>


00:23:14.960 --> 00:23:17.400
<i>has said the president
is most concerned about the break-in</i>


00:23:17.480 --> 00:23:20.600
<i>and will be keeping
a very close eye on the investigation.</i>


00:23:20.680 --> 00:23:22.444
<i>Now, turning to other news...</i>


00:23:24.080 --> 00:23:25.730
Mr. Lano is running street on this.


00:23:26.640 --> 00:23:28.440
2:15, Sunday morning,


00:23:28.520 --> 00:23:32.002
Metro finds our perps inside the
Democratic National Committee office.


00:23:32.320 --> 00:23:35.440
We ID'd the lead. He's a pro.


00:23:35.520 --> 00:23:38.922
Five years in the FBI, 19 in the CIA.


00:23:39.840 --> 00:23:43.128
Then he left the CIA to run security
for the Attorney General.


00:23:43.560 --> 00:23:46.000
Then he ran security for the White House


00:23:46.080 --> 00:23:47.880
for the Committee to Re-elect the President.


00:23:47.960 --> 00:23:50.600
The lead burglar ran security for the
Committee to Re-elect the President?


00:23:50.680 --> 00:23:53.680
- Is that what you said?
- That's what he said. Keep going.


00:23:53.760 --> 00:23:55.000
Yeah, it gets weirder.


00:23:55.120 --> 00:23:57.600
The lookout in here, three years FBI.


00:23:57.680 --> 00:24:01.287
Then the Attorney General recruits him
to be his wife's personal bodyguard.


00:24:06.160 --> 00:24:07.400
Just keep going.


00:24:07.560 --> 00:24:10.405
The lookout makes a Howard Hunt
the ringleader.


00:24:10.560 --> 00:24:12.160
Hunt's also ex-CIA.


00:24:12.240 --> 00:24:13.241
But get this,


00:24:13.440 --> 00:24:15.200
a year ago we were asked to do
a background check


00:24:15.280 --> 00:24:16.440
on Hunt for a government job.


00:24:16.520 --> 00:24:18.648
- Did we clear him?
- Yeah.


00:24:18.880 --> 00:24:20.840
For a job at the White House


00:24:20.920 --> 00:24:24.720
as a "consultant on highly sensitive,
confidential matters."


00:24:26.400 --> 00:24:28.209
That's a job title?


00:24:32.280 --> 00:24:34.960
White House, Justice and the CIA


00:24:35.040 --> 00:24:37.646
are gonna want to know everything we know.


00:24:40.120 --> 00:24:42.566
But we aren't going to tell them. Anything.


00:24:42.720 --> 00:24:44.609
The Attorney General already called.


00:24:44.800 --> 00:24:46.720
Nobody talks to the Attorney General.


00:24:46.800 --> 00:24:49.645
- We answer to the Attorney General.
- You answer to me.


00:24:51.040 --> 00:24:52.849
What about the director?


00:24:53.120 --> 00:24:55.327
I'll take care of the director.


00:24:56.160 --> 00:24:59.040
<i>There is still no explanation
why the Watergate suspects</i>


00:24:59.120 --> 00:25:01.320
<i>might have attempted
to bug Democratic headquarters.</i>


00:25:01.400 --> 00:25:03.760
<i>A spokesman for the Attorney General
said yesterday</i>


00:25:03.840 --> 00:25:05.760
<i>that the FBI is already investigating.</i>


00:25:05.840 --> 00:25:09.322
<i>Their report will be turned over to the
criminal division for appropriate...</i>


00:25:31.000 --> 00:25:34.925
John Dean, the president's counsel,
just went into the director's office.


00:25:35.960 --> 00:25:38.486
- Let me know when he comes out.
- Yes, Mr. Felt.


00:25:51.160 --> 00:25:52.890
<i>Mr. Dean has left.</i>


00:25:53.080 --> 00:25:55.083
<i>The director's leaving in a bit to play golf.</i>


00:26:01.800 --> 00:26:04.451
What's John Dean doing here in this building?


00:26:08.400 --> 00:26:12.121
This is a remarkable amount of information


00:26:12.480 --> 00:26:14.000
about the break-in.


00:26:14.080 --> 00:26:17.209
We're still gathering string.
This is just the beginning.


00:26:17.600 --> 00:26:19.170
Okay.


00:26:21.480 --> 00:26:23.926
First of all, there are no more interviews


00:26:24.040 --> 00:26:27.240
with White House or CIA people
without permission.


00:26:27.320 --> 00:26:29.129
- What?
- Whose permission?


00:26:32.120 --> 00:26:34.009
Give us a minute.


00:26:37.680 --> 00:26:39.410
Get out.


00:26:42.640 --> 00:26:44.768
The FBI is an independent body.


00:26:44.960 --> 00:26:46.080
I'm aware of that.


00:26:46.160 --> 00:26:48.760
Are you also aware that means
we don't need permission


00:26:48.840 --> 00:26:50.922
to do anything from anybody?


00:26:51.680 --> 00:26:55.280
You give that up just one time,
you don't ever get it back. Ever.


00:26:55.360 --> 00:26:57.320
Let's not get dramatic.
We don't even know what this is.


00:26:57.400 --> 00:26:59.320
That's right. We don't.


00:26:59.400 --> 00:27:02.051
But we're going to find out.
That's what we do.


00:27:02.840 --> 00:27:04.920
You don't work for them.


00:27:05.000 --> 00:27:07.571
You're the director of the FBI now.


00:27:17.680 --> 00:27:19.364
Forty-eight hours.


00:27:21.160 --> 00:27:24.562
We put the investigation to bed
and get on with the rest of our lives


00:27:24.960 --> 00:27:26.610
in two days.


00:27:29.520 --> 00:27:31.602
You've got 48 hours.


00:27:33.320 --> 00:27:34.651
Thank you.


00:28:18.960 --> 00:28:20.560
Nice to see you.


00:28:20.640 --> 00:28:22.404
What brings you back?


00:28:23.400 --> 00:28:24.925
Two words.


00:28:26.080 --> 00:28:27.764
Re... Venge.


00:29:08.480 --> 00:29:11.211
- Was everything all right, Daniel?
- It's great as always.


00:29:11.320 --> 00:29:14.881
- Your total's going to be $47.70.
- Thanks, darlin'.


00:29:16.200 --> 00:29:17.850
There you go. I'll see you next time.


00:29:18.040 --> 00:29:19.485
Say hi to your mama.


00:29:26.720 --> 00:29:28.529
You look like hell.


00:29:31.480 --> 00:29:32.720
Have some food.


00:29:32.800 --> 00:29:35.007
- How are you, sir?
- Just coffee, thanks.


00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:42.320
So, what does this look like to you, Sandy,


00:29:42.400 --> 00:29:44.120
and your pals at <i>Time</i> magazine?


00:29:44.200 --> 00:29:45.930
The Watergate thing?


00:29:48.280 --> 00:29:49.486
Honestly, I...


00:29:51.120 --> 00:29:54.044
No one at <i>Time</i> magazine or any newspaper
I know can figure it out.


00:29:54.800 --> 00:29:57.770
Ex-spooks get caught planting bugs?


00:30:04.520 --> 00:30:06.887
Does have a particular odor to it though.


00:30:16.640 --> 00:30:20.440
I bet your old pal Bill Sullivan
sure misses the FBI.


00:30:23.320 --> 00:30:27.400
Because I heard the White House
gave him some bullshit job,


00:30:27.480 --> 00:30:28.891
waiting for Hoover to kick off.


00:30:29.720 --> 00:30:31.848
Sullivan wants back in.


00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:35.322
The president wants him back in
to run the FBI their way.


00:30:38.440 --> 00:30:40.443
Nixon and Sullivan.


00:30:42.240 --> 00:30:43.810
Those two are made for each other.


00:30:48.640 --> 00:30:50.005
Here you go.


00:30:52.600 --> 00:30:54.364
Could we have some pie, please?


00:30:54.720 --> 00:30:57.160
What kind? We have apple, blueberry...


00:30:57.240 --> 00:30:58.367
You pick.


00:31:00.360 --> 00:31:02.363
What are we doing out here, Mark?


00:31:05.000 --> 00:31:06.889
I was given 48 hours.


00:31:08.880 --> 00:31:10.211
To do what?


00:31:11.880 --> 00:31:14.247
Wrap up the Watergate investigation.


00:31:15.840 --> 00:31:17.365
By who?


00:31:20.600 --> 00:31:22.125
Gray?


00:31:24.600 --> 00:31:27.649
Pat Gray, the director of the FBI,


00:31:28.520 --> 00:31:31.330
ordered the FBI
to stop its own investigation?


00:31:32.320 --> 00:31:34.400
There are calls we are not allowed to make


00:31:34.480 --> 00:31:37.370
and phone and bank records we can't go near.


00:31:40.800 --> 00:31:42.450
Thank you.


00:31:56.400 --> 00:32:01.008
In all the years I've known you,
you've never given up a single,


00:32:01.120 --> 00:32:02.929
real secret.


00:32:06.320 --> 00:32:08.050
Nothing but the company line.


00:32:12.920 --> 00:32:15.366
These are uncharted waters for you.


00:32:20.760 --> 00:32:22.842
So, one more time. What are we doing?


00:32:23.960 --> 00:32:26.008
You looking for a little help?


00:32:27.040 --> 00:32:28.087
Payback?


00:32:28.840 --> 00:32:31.571
I want the FBI left alone to do its job.


00:32:33.280 --> 00:32:35.010
That's all I want.


00:32:36.280 --> 00:32:39.011
And you want me to light a fire
around the edges


00:32:40.040 --> 00:32:41.041
with a story.


00:32:43.440 --> 00:32:45.647
Well, I can see why
they didn't give you the job.


00:32:50.080 --> 00:32:52.242
They must be terrified of you.


00:33:28.480 --> 00:33:30.926
- Come on, come on.
- <i>Washington Post.</i>


00:34:00.400 --> 00:34:03.051
I miss you.
I know I'm not supposed to say that.


00:34:04.560 --> 00:34:06.722
- It is okay to say that.
- No.


00:34:08.080 --> 00:34:09.650
It's too touchy-feely.


00:34:10.640 --> 00:34:12.688
I need you too much.


00:34:14.720 --> 00:34:16.563
Where were you tonight?


00:34:16.760 --> 00:34:19.081
The switchboard said
they didn't know where you were.


00:34:19.720 --> 00:34:22.160
Because I didn't tell them.


00:34:22.240 --> 00:34:24.083
Well, what about Mrs. Tschudy?


00:34:24.680 --> 00:34:26.091
She didn't know either.


00:34:27.600 --> 00:34:30.445
But you taught her
to always say that, didn't you?


00:34:39.040 --> 00:34:41.441
Have you been making the calls about Joan?


00:34:42.920 --> 00:34:44.570
I've called all her friends.


00:34:45.000 --> 00:34:48.971
They haven't heard from her in nearly a year.


00:34:54.400 --> 00:34:55.845
Are you looking for her?


00:34:57.320 --> 00:34:59.640
Is the most powerful law enforcement agency


00:34:59.720 --> 00:35:01.440
in the world looking for her?


00:35:01.520 --> 00:35:03.011
I can't do that.


00:35:05.920 --> 00:35:07.729
It's against the rules?


00:35:12.760 --> 00:35:15.286
We don't know what they will find.


00:35:16.880 --> 00:35:17.881
Do we?


00:36:21.080 --> 00:36:23.083
Where the hell did they get that?


00:36:48.280 --> 00:36:49.400
Mr. Bates.


00:36:49.480 --> 00:36:52.928
This <i>Washington Post</i> story says
we know who the Watergate ringleader is.


00:36:53.920 --> 00:36:57.760
Then, this morning,
our <i>Time</i> magazine pal, Sandy Smith,


00:36:57.840 --> 00:37:01.400
called the acting director
to say that he is prepping a story


00:37:01.480 --> 00:37:03.960
that the FBI is plotting a whitewash.


00:37:04.040 --> 00:37:08.728
He said the director has put
a 48-hour cap on the investigation.


00:37:09.280 --> 00:37:11.120
- What's your point?
- Is that true?


00:37:11.200 --> 00:37:13.960
Someone in this office
is talking to the press.


00:37:14.040 --> 00:37:15.640
The point, Mr. Lano,


00:37:15.720 --> 00:37:17.440
is that leaks kill investigations.


00:37:17.520 --> 00:37:19.680
- Okay. Okay.
- Take it down, Angie.


00:37:19.760 --> 00:37:23.000
You want to conduct
a leak investigation, be my guest.


00:37:23.080 --> 00:37:26.368
But you got 200 field agents from
here to LA all chasing down leads,


00:37:26.520 --> 00:37:28.240
so you're gonna have to ask them all, too.


00:37:28.320 --> 00:37:30.040
Tone, in front of Mr. Felt.


00:37:30.120 --> 00:37:33.886
I can guarantee it wasn't me
or any of the guys in this room.


00:37:34.000 --> 00:37:36.480
Donald H. Segretti.


00:37:36.760 --> 00:37:39.120
You pulled that name
from Howard Hunt's phone records.


00:37:39.200 --> 00:37:40.964
He called Hunt a few dozen times, yeah.


00:37:41.200 --> 00:37:44.648
This says Segretti used to be a lawyer
in the Treasury Department,


00:37:44.800 --> 00:37:47.087
paid out of the account
that funded the Watergate.


00:37:47.200 --> 00:37:50.443
An account belonging to
the Committee to Re-elect the President.


00:37:50.560 --> 00:37:52.480
- Who is the head of the committee?
- John Mitchell.


00:37:52.560 --> 00:37:55.370
Former Attorney General, John Mitchell.


00:37:55.880 --> 00:37:58.611
The best we can make out is
Segretti's some kind of prankster.


00:37:58.760 --> 00:38:02.800
You know, like he's spying on the Dems,
sending their wives dirty pictures.


00:38:02.880 --> 00:38:05.920
- It's all bottom-feeder, frat boy stuff.
- Indictable under election laws.


00:38:06.000 --> 00:38:07.800
Forget the plot of the story, Mr. Kunkel.


00:38:07.880 --> 00:38:10.040
What's the theme? What's it saying?
What does it mean?


00:38:10.120 --> 00:38:12.960
Like Angie, like Mr. Lano said,
we are still vetting the leads.


00:38:13.040 --> 00:38:16.931
All the ugly politics,
all the dirty money, all the sleaze.


00:38:17.040 --> 00:38:20.044
It means the goddamn punks
are running the country!


00:38:28.200 --> 00:38:29.327
Keep going.


00:38:30.880 --> 00:38:33.690
You might want to talk to
the White House about those leaks.


00:38:38.600 --> 00:38:40.400
- Why?
- 'Cause whenever I'm lucky enough


00:38:40.480 --> 00:38:42.528
to get someone over there
to actually talk to me,


00:38:42.960 --> 00:38:45.566
they know what I'm gonna ask before I ask it.


00:38:47.640 --> 00:38:49.608
It's like they already know
what I want to know.


00:38:57.480 --> 00:39:00.802
Mr. Felt, I have the White House
on the phone. Mr. John Dean.


00:39:20.720 --> 00:39:21.926
Put him through.


00:39:25.680 --> 00:39:26.807
Mr. Dean.


00:39:26.920 --> 00:39:29.366
<i>The White House is concerned
about these press leaks.</i>


00:39:31.840 --> 00:39:33.320
Of course.


00:39:33.400 --> 00:39:36.643
<i>We think the source
must be someone in the FBI.</i>


00:39:42.880 --> 00:39:44.883
Why FBI?


00:39:45.080 --> 00:39:47.287
<i>That's where the information is.</i>


00:39:48.400 --> 00:39:51.370
Those stories could have come
from someone in the White House.


00:39:54.760 --> 00:39:57.080
We want you to do something
about it, Mr. Felt.


00:39:57.160 --> 00:39:59.402
- <i>Okay.</i>
- Now.


00:39:59.800 --> 00:40:01.245
Fine.


00:40:01.400 --> 00:40:02.845
But I don't understand.


00:40:04.240 --> 00:40:06.971
- Which part?
- The part about you calling me.


00:40:07.400 --> 00:40:10.529
The White House
has no authority over the FBI.


00:40:14.680 --> 00:40:17.889
- We can...
- At all, Mr. Dean.


00:40:20.960 --> 00:40:22.325
But we can suggest...


00:40:22.440 --> 00:40:25.922
I'm afraid the White House
has nothing to suggest to the FBI.


00:40:29.720 --> 00:40:32.883
- <i>Thank you, Mr. Felt.</i>
- Thank you, Mr. Dean.


00:41:01.200 --> 00:41:05.205
I want you to disappear
our investigation on these two names.


00:41:05.440 --> 00:41:07.560
Get them off the interview list.


00:41:07.640 --> 00:41:09.244
I don't get it. They're nobody.


00:41:09.360 --> 00:41:10.771
Just do it.


00:41:15.160 --> 00:41:18.801
Then make sure you say you did it
in Monday's memo for the director.


00:41:25.920 --> 00:41:27.126
Thank you.


00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:32.287
Your daily Watergate briefing.


00:41:34.640 --> 00:41:37.689
Thanks, Charlie. May I call you Charlie?


00:41:39.440 --> 00:41:42.762
How much of what we are getting
on Watergate am I actually seeing?


00:41:45.120 --> 00:41:47.160
Mr. Felt gives me the headlines.
I type them up.


00:41:47.240 --> 00:41:50.323
I give Mr. Felt the original
and bring you a copy.


00:41:51.360 --> 00:41:53.931
Mr. Felt doesn't want
to waste your time with details.


00:42:01.400 --> 00:42:02.845
Okay.


00:42:03.800 --> 00:42:05.211
Okay, Mr. Gray.


00:42:17.840 --> 00:42:19.205
Mr. Kunkel!


00:42:20.720 --> 00:42:23.240
Director Gray wanted you to know
he understands you and your boys


00:42:23.320 --> 00:42:24.765
are doing a hell of a job.


00:42:25.200 --> 00:42:28.680
Well, thank Mr. Gray, and not to worry.
We'll gather the whole ball of yarn.


00:42:28.760 --> 00:42:30.440
Mr. Gray also wanted you to know


00:42:30.520 --> 00:42:35.242
that there was gonna be a small change
in procedure in the information flow.


00:42:35.720 --> 00:42:38.803
How and, more precisely, where it flows.


00:42:39.040 --> 00:42:42.010
Not just the headlines, but the story itself.


00:42:42.320 --> 00:42:44.482
The details, as it were.


00:42:46.120 --> 00:42:48.202
Does Mr. Felt know?


00:42:49.520 --> 00:42:50.965
Of course.


00:43:46.200 --> 00:43:48.407
Angie Lano called me last night.


00:43:49.720 --> 00:43:51.370
He told me that he called the White House


00:43:51.480 --> 00:43:53.448
to set up a round of interviews.


00:43:53.800 --> 00:43:56.080
Half hour later the White House called back


00:43:56.160 --> 00:43:59.084
to tell me that we can't talk
to two of the guys


00:43:59.480 --> 00:44:01.960
because their names were taken off the list.


00:44:02.920 --> 00:44:04.445
The two names you told me.


00:44:05.760 --> 00:44:07.763
How would the White House know?


00:44:08.720 --> 00:44:10.768
I guess somebody told them.


00:44:12.120 --> 00:44:14.885
The only people who knew were me and you.


00:44:16.200 --> 00:44:17.691
And Mr. Gray.


00:44:19.480 --> 00:44:20.925
And Mr. Gray.


00:44:23.760 --> 00:44:25.888
We need to find out what Gray has,


00:44:27.200 --> 00:44:28.884
and how he's getting it.


00:44:32.960 --> 00:44:34.960
Did I do something wrong?


00:44:35.040 --> 00:44:36.610
Mr. Bates tells me


00:44:37.640 --> 00:44:41.406
you've been giving Mr. Gray everything
we're collecting on Watergate.


00:44:42.320 --> 00:44:44.607
All our interviews, all of our files.


00:44:46.760 --> 00:44:49.491
Did Mr. Gray tell you to bypass me?


00:44:49.640 --> 00:44:51.688
Well, he didn't say
it was a secret or anything.


00:44:54.960 --> 00:44:56.963
But he said that you knew.


00:44:58.840 --> 00:45:01.760
How often did you give him our files?


00:45:01.840 --> 00:45:03.524
- Every day.
- Why?


00:45:05.080 --> 00:45:07.083
We know why.


00:45:11.680 --> 00:45:15.120
Did you give the Attorney General
any information about our investigation?


00:45:15.200 --> 00:45:17.680
- I don't talk to the Attorney General.
- Did you, Mr. Bates?


00:45:19.040 --> 00:45:20.531
Mr. Miller?


00:45:25.960 --> 00:45:27.963
The Attorney General called me this morning


00:45:28.120 --> 00:45:31.488
about something
he could only have heard from the FBI.


00:45:38.560 --> 00:45:40.688
He's putting a box around Watergate.


00:45:42.560 --> 00:45:45.480
We can't touch anything before the break-in.


00:45:45.560 --> 00:45:49.167
We have to stay away
from all the White House corruption.


00:45:49.800 --> 00:45:53.521
In other words,
the crimes that matter don't matter.


00:45:54.280 --> 00:45:57.523
For the first time in its history, the FBI


00:45:58.680 --> 00:46:00.680
has been quarantined.


00:46:00.760 --> 00:46:04.731
Crimes that it knows about
will go uninvestigated.


00:46:09.160 --> 00:46:11.811
- Mr. Felt...
- Thank you, Mr. Kunkel.


00:46:25.080 --> 00:46:28.243
So, with everything we have right now,


00:46:29.840 --> 00:46:31.922
if we could get indictments,


00:46:33.760 --> 00:46:37.242
in your opinion, who would we get?


00:46:38.320 --> 00:46:39.651
How high?


00:46:42.880 --> 00:46:44.769
Maybe Attorney General.


00:46:48.480 --> 00:46:50.005
What about the president?


00:46:54.960 --> 00:46:56.769
What about the president?


00:46:57.520 --> 00:46:59.807
If the president's lying...


00:47:01.760 --> 00:47:03.560
Is the president lying?


00:47:03.640 --> 00:47:05.324
They're all lying.


00:47:07.800 --> 00:47:09.086
Then, yes.


00:47:11.880 --> 00:47:13.245
Maybe the president.


00:47:15.440 --> 00:47:17.520
<i>As the investigations went forward,</i>


00:47:17.600 --> 00:47:22.367
<i>I repeatedly asked
those conducting the investigation</i>


00:47:22.480 --> 00:47:24.800
<i>whether there was any reason to believe</i>


00:47:24.880 --> 00:47:28.965
<i>that members of my administration
were in any way involved.</i>


00:47:29.800 --> 00:47:34.124
<i>I received repeated assurances
that there were none.</i>


00:47:34.440 --> 00:47:36.682
<i>I discounted the stories in the press.</i>


00:47:36.880 --> 00:47:39.565
<i>Who do you think gave the orders
to bug the Watergate?</i>


00:47:39.800 --> 00:47:44.761
<i>Well, the persons who the grand jury
indicted in Washington, DC, last week,</i>


00:47:44.920 --> 00:47:46.480
<i>gave the orders to do it.</i>


00:47:46.560 --> 00:47:48.051
<i>You don't think
they were following orders, then?</i>


00:47:48.240 --> 00:47:49.960
- <i>No, I do not.</i>
- <i>There's nobody higher?</i>


00:47:50.040 --> 00:47:52.088
<i>There has been no evidence
presented that anybody did that.</i>


00:47:52.200 --> 00:47:54.880
<i>I think the opposition is disappointed</i>


00:47:54.960 --> 00:47:57.680
<i>that after such a thorough,
intensive investigation</i>


00:47:57.760 --> 00:48:00.240
<i>that just seven persons were indicted.</i>


00:48:00.320 --> 00:48:02.840
<i>The Watergate break-in took a dramatic turn</i>


00:48:02.920 --> 00:48:04.120
<i>when one of the defendants,</i>


00:48:04.200 --> 00:48:06.480
former White House consultant E. Howard Hunt,


00:48:06.560 --> 00:48:07.840
changed his plea to guilty.


00:48:07.920 --> 00:48:10.840
<i>The judge accepted the guilty pleas
of the four Miami men</i>


00:48:10.920 --> 00:48:13.160
<i>on the condition
that they answer his questions</i>


00:48:13.240 --> 00:48:15.520
<i>on who else was involved in Watergate.</i>


00:48:15.600 --> 00:48:19.760
<i>With the crucial questions
of who, and what, were behind it all</i>


00:48:19.840 --> 00:48:20.967
<i>still unanswered.</i>


00:48:22.680 --> 00:48:24.648
<i>I got a call from across the river.</i>


00:48:25.720 --> 00:48:28.405
- <i>Which river is that?</i>
- <i>The Potomac.</i>


00:48:28.640 --> 00:48:29.971
The CIA.


00:48:30.960 --> 00:48:33.440
The CIA is telling us we need to taper off.


00:48:33.520 --> 00:48:35.250
Taper off?


00:48:36.080 --> 00:48:38.840
- We're getting too close.
- Too close to what?


00:48:38.920 --> 00:48:39.920
I can't tell you.


00:48:40.000 --> 00:48:42.040
You can't, or you won't?


00:48:42.120 --> 00:48:44.123
It's a matter of national security.


00:48:44.280 --> 00:48:48.604
<i>We are doing everything that we can
to investigate this incident.</i>


00:48:48.880 --> 00:48:52.440
<i>No one on the White House staff,
no one in this administration</i>


00:48:52.520 --> 00:48:56.241
<i>was involved in this very bizarre incident.</i>


00:48:56.960 --> 00:48:59.531
<i>The CIA is telling us we need to taper off.</i>


00:49:00.280 --> 00:49:02.360
<i>Disappointed. Disappointed.</i>


00:49:02.440 --> 00:49:04.480
<i>No one in this administration...</i>


00:49:04.560 --> 00:49:07.882
- <i>We're getting too close.</i>
- <i>It's a matter of national security.</i>


00:49:11.480 --> 00:49:14.240
<i>A bomb exploded early this morning
in the Pentagon</i>


00:49:14.320 --> 00:49:16.527
<i>and left-wing terrorists
telephoned newspapers</i>


00:49:16.640 --> 00:49:18.005
<i>to say they were responsible.</i>


00:49:19.800 --> 00:49:21.320
<i>People calling themselves members
of the Weather Underground...</i>


00:49:21.400 --> 00:49:22.800
- Yes?
- <i>Are you watching this?</i>


00:49:22.880 --> 00:49:24.120
I see it.


00:49:25.000 --> 00:49:27.520
- <i>What about the White House?</i>
- It's at the top of their list.


00:49:27.600 --> 00:49:29.120
I told you that three months ago.


00:49:29.200 --> 00:49:33.808
- But can they really hit it?
- They just hit the Pentagon.


00:49:34.200 --> 00:49:36.089
I want us to open files on every member


00:49:36.200 --> 00:49:38.840
of every counterculture organization
in the country.


00:49:38.920 --> 00:49:41.446
<i>Hunt them to exhaustion. No holds barred.</i>


00:49:41.960 --> 00:49:44.440
The president is fighting
for the White House.


00:49:44.640 --> 00:49:46.290
That's not my job.


00:49:46.520 --> 00:49:47.960
The president needs order.


00:49:48.040 --> 00:49:50.566
I promised the president he'd have order.


00:49:53.640 --> 00:49:56.325
Which brings me to my next point, Felt.


00:49:57.800 --> 00:50:00.121
I spoke to the Attorney General.


00:50:01.680 --> 00:50:04.604
The Attorney General
is going to officially announce


00:50:04.760 --> 00:50:08.080
we have found nothing
connecting the president on Watergate.


00:50:08.160 --> 00:50:10.640
What? But that's not real.


00:50:10.720 --> 00:50:15.601
I know. And the president knows
you are still pursuing it.


00:50:18.080 --> 00:50:20.200
<i>You're never going to find
what you're chasing.</i>


00:50:20.280 --> 00:50:22.931
<i>I want it to end. It's time to finish it.</i>


00:50:23.040 --> 00:50:24.690
<i>Shut it down.</i>


00:50:27.200 --> 00:50:30.124
I hear you and your wife
are registered Democrats, Mark.


00:50:30.960 --> 00:50:32.644
I hope you're not going
to let that get in the way.


00:50:37.680 --> 00:50:40.160
<i>The Weather Underground, they're combining.</i>


00:50:40.240 --> 00:50:42.000
They're multiplying.


00:50:42.080 --> 00:50:43.640
We'll never get warrants. Not now.


00:50:43.720 --> 00:50:44.721
Warrants?


00:50:45.040 --> 00:50:48.000
We're not talking about the kids
sleeping out there in the parks.


00:50:48.080 --> 00:50:51.960
We're talking about people who would
burn your children alive in their beds.


00:50:52.040 --> 00:50:55.400
People die because we stick to the
letter of the law, we lose everything,


00:50:55.480 --> 00:50:56.481
including the law.


00:50:57.480 --> 00:50:58.641
We're taking off the gloves.


00:50:59.360 --> 00:51:01.720
Entries, taps, nothing on paper.


00:51:01.800 --> 00:51:03.600
No warrants.


00:51:03.680 --> 00:51:05.520
Mr. Miller's people report to Mr. Miller.


00:51:05.600 --> 00:51:06.760
Mr. Miller reports to me.


00:51:06.840 --> 00:51:08.444
Just like the bad old days.


00:51:08.760 --> 00:51:10.680
Where's Bill Sullivan when you need him?


00:51:10.760 --> 00:51:12.320
He's over at the White House,


00:51:12.400 --> 00:51:16.087
protecting the nation by
spying on senators and their mistresses


00:51:16.320 --> 00:51:19.961
while we're here just trying to
keep all this goddamn mess together.


00:51:26.840 --> 00:51:28.080
Hey, look.


00:51:29.680 --> 00:51:31.330
We're on your side here.


00:51:31.800 --> 00:51:33.928
All I'm saying is, all that was behind us.


00:51:34.160 --> 00:51:35.800
Even Hoover knew the dirty stuff was over.


00:51:35.880 --> 00:51:37.291
That's why Bill's gone.


00:51:38.280 --> 00:51:41.170
All I'm saying is, everyone is watching.


00:51:41.440 --> 00:51:44.046
How many more kids do we have to lose?


00:51:44.160 --> 00:51:47.130
How many more
do we let just vanish into eternity?


00:51:47.840 --> 00:51:50.440
I am not Bill Sullivan.


00:51:50.520 --> 00:51:52.966
This is still the goddamn FBI.


00:52:15.560 --> 00:52:16.925
I don't want to intrude.


00:52:18.320 --> 00:52:19.447
Then don't.


00:52:24.080 --> 00:52:25.161
You heard from her?


00:52:26.760 --> 00:52:28.046
Joan.


00:52:31.240 --> 00:52:33.561
You think she's involved with all this?


00:52:34.680 --> 00:52:35.920
The Underground?


00:52:37.600 --> 00:52:38.931
How could she?


00:52:39.640 --> 00:52:41.920
She's just like me. Exactly like me.


00:52:42.000 --> 00:52:43.240
She worships you.


00:52:49.680 --> 00:52:50.727
She's okay.


00:52:52.880 --> 00:52:54.120
I can feel it, Mark.


00:52:57.240 --> 00:52:59.811
There's a price to pay for what we do,
Mr. Miller.


00:52:59.920 --> 00:53:02.162
There's a price to pay for what we become.


00:53:04.200 --> 00:53:06.407
We all pay it, one way or another.


00:53:09.120 --> 00:53:14.570
<i>Watergate was the most intensive,
objective and thorough investigation</i>


00:53:14.960 --> 00:53:19.602
<i>in the history of the
US attorney's office and the FBI.</i>


00:53:21.760 --> 00:53:24.160
<i>The Justice Department has now completed</i>


00:53:24.240 --> 00:53:26.527
<i>its criminal investigation</i>


00:53:26.640 --> 00:53:29.962
<i>without implicating any present official</i>


00:53:30.560 --> 00:53:32.164
<i>of either the White House</i>


00:53:32.680 --> 00:53:35.729
<i>or the Committee to Re-elect the President.</i>


00:53:36.040 --> 00:53:37.326
- Completed?
- <i>Any questions?</i>


00:53:37.440 --> 00:53:38.680
What the hell, man?


00:53:39.200 --> 00:53:40.680
Get me Felt on the phone.


00:53:40.760 --> 00:53:42.520
- <i>As to the White House?</i>
- Hold on, hold on. Wait a second.


00:53:42.600 --> 00:53:47.520
<i>I understand the FBI's Watergate
investigation is in a state of repose</i>


00:53:47.600 --> 00:53:48.647
<i>and unlikely to be reopened.</i>


00:53:49.840 --> 00:53:51.683
Anybody tell us this was over yet?


00:53:52.280 --> 00:53:55.090
Get me Felt on the phone! Or Bates!


00:53:56.400 --> 00:53:57.811
God damn it, get me Felt!


00:53:58.080 --> 00:53:59.320
- She can't.
- Why the hell not?


00:53:59.440 --> 00:54:00.480
'Cause he's right there.


00:54:00.560 --> 00:54:04.326
<i>And now, let's return to the press
conference of the US Attorney General.</i>


00:54:51.280 --> 00:54:52.486
Maybe she's dead.


00:54:56.600 --> 00:54:58.250
Maybe she just gave up.


00:54:59.240 --> 00:55:01.004
Didn't think anybody cared.


00:55:04.080 --> 00:55:06.367
Maybe she's right out there watching us.


00:55:07.560 --> 00:55:11.920
To see what a man like you does when
your daughter just vanishes one night


00:55:12.000 --> 00:55:13.480
for no good reason.


00:55:13.560 --> 00:55:15.085
Joan had a reason for everything.


00:55:16.120 --> 00:55:17.247
You hated her.


00:55:23.200 --> 00:55:25.009
Mothers don't hate their daughters.


00:55:26.760 --> 00:55:29.002
It's just not always easy being one.


00:55:29.600 --> 00:55:31.568
You dressed her up like a doll,


00:55:32.440 --> 00:55:34.760
until she got old enough
to look just like you.


00:55:34.840 --> 00:55:35.840
Mark.


00:55:35.920 --> 00:55:38.560
You kept telling her to get out
until one day she listened to you.


00:55:38.640 --> 00:55:39.846
Listen to me.


00:55:41.400 --> 00:55:42.760
I had no mother.


00:55:42.840 --> 00:55:44.200
But she did.


00:55:44.280 --> 00:55:45.486
Yes.


00:55:46.360 --> 00:55:47.441
She did.


00:55:48.400 --> 00:55:49.811
My father just left.


00:55:51.680 --> 00:55:53.569
So, yes, she gave me up


00:55:54.760 --> 00:55:56.444
to foster homes,


00:55:56.960 --> 00:55:58.690
then the orphanage.


00:56:01.280 --> 00:56:03.328
- But you know all about that, don't you?
- Yeah.


00:56:10.280 --> 00:56:12.089
Then I made my own way.


00:56:14.400 --> 00:56:15.731
Until you.


00:56:16.760 --> 00:56:18.125
My white knight.


00:56:21.120 --> 00:56:24.169
Our homes are the only homes I've ever known.


00:56:32.640 --> 00:56:34.483
You were both mine.


00:56:38.200 --> 00:56:39.201
<i>How's home, Mark?</i>


00:56:42.800 --> 00:56:44.006
Why are you asking?


00:56:44.720 --> 00:56:46.484
That daughter of yours, Jill?


00:56:48.280 --> 00:56:49.281
Joan.


00:56:50.320 --> 00:56:51.811
Well, I hear she's terrific.


00:56:53.040 --> 00:56:56.044
Fulbright scholar, first girl in the country.


00:56:57.840 --> 00:56:59.410
A chip off the old block.


00:57:06.120 --> 00:57:09.602
I want you to be the first
to hear my statement to the press.


00:57:15.080 --> 00:57:16.889
"No pressure has been put on me


00:57:17.720 --> 00:57:21.080
"or any of my special agents
in the FBI's investigation


00:57:21.160 --> 00:57:24.608
"and that it strains..." I thought
I would just nip this in the bud.


00:57:25.160 --> 00:57:27.766
"It strains credulity that President Nixon


00:57:27.880 --> 00:57:30.281
"could have done a con job
on the whole American people."


00:57:32.880 --> 00:57:34.291
What do you think?


00:57:37.120 --> 00:57:38.645
It's just fine.


00:57:43.640 --> 00:57:46.246
The Democrats
have issued a statement this morning.


00:57:48.120 --> 00:57:52.011
"The FBI's Watergate investigation
is a whitewash.


00:57:54.600 --> 00:57:58.844
"What is involved here is not only
the political life of this nation


00:57:59.800 --> 00:58:03.771
"but the very morality of our leaders


00:58:05.040 --> 00:58:08.680
"at a time when the United States
desperately needs to revitalize


00:58:08.760 --> 00:58:10.967
"its moral standards."


00:58:13.840 --> 00:58:17.288
"The FBI's Watergate investigation


00:58:19.800 --> 00:58:21.245
"is a whitewash."


00:58:25.600 --> 00:58:26.886
That's it.


00:58:33.200 --> 00:58:34.880
Well, gentlemen.


00:58:34.960 --> 00:58:36.485
Here's what we know.


00:58:37.720 --> 00:58:40.240
We know what we've heard
out of the Department of Justice


00:58:40.320 --> 00:58:42.209
the past two days is bullshit.


00:58:44.680 --> 00:58:47.720
We know the men who broke into the Watergate


00:58:47.800 --> 00:58:49.484
are not the end of this thing,


00:58:51.160 --> 00:58:52.605
but the beginning.


00:58:53.560 --> 00:58:55.280
We know this is the latest link


00:58:55.360 --> 00:59:00.400
in a chain of illegal,
covert intelligence operations


00:59:00.800 --> 00:59:02.848
by the president's re-election campaign.


00:59:03.960 --> 00:59:07.280
We know we are facing obstruction
from multiple fronts.


00:59:07.360 --> 00:59:08.771
From the White House.


00:59:09.160 --> 00:59:10.651
From the CIA.


00:59:11.760 --> 00:59:14.360
From the Attorney General
of the United States,


00:59:14.440 --> 00:59:17.125
who is our boss, by the way.


00:59:18.320 --> 00:59:21.768
It is not our job to speculate
on the involvement of the president.


00:59:24.240 --> 00:59:26.607
It is our job to follow the bread crumbs.


00:59:27.840 --> 00:59:31.280
But those bread crumbs appear to be taking us


00:59:31.360 --> 00:59:33.886
on a tour of the West Wing
of the White House,


00:59:35.800 --> 00:59:38.565
and in the general direction
of the Oval Office.


00:59:40.280 --> 00:59:44.640
We also know we've been ordered
to shut down our pursuit of all this


00:59:44.720 --> 00:59:46.245
as of today.


00:59:47.960 --> 00:59:50.850
And we know that except
for the 30 men in this room,


00:59:52.520 --> 00:59:55.960
no one in the entire country
knows any of this


00:59:56.040 --> 00:59:58.566
and may never know any of this.


01:00:02.720 --> 01:00:06.247
No one can stop the driving force
of an FBI investigation.


01:00:06.920 --> 01:00:08.923
Not even the FBI.


01:00:37.880 --> 01:00:39.086
Segretti.


01:01:17.160 --> 01:01:18.840
I'm going to give you the name of a man


01:01:18.920 --> 01:01:21.287
who was asked to work
for the Nixon administration


01:01:22.240 --> 01:01:23.731
in an unusual way.


01:01:24.640 --> 01:01:25.687
<i>What are you talking about?</i>


01:01:26.680 --> 01:01:29.880
There's only one way to understand
what Watergate really means,


01:01:29.960 --> 01:01:31.166
and this is it.


01:01:33.240 --> 01:01:34.287
The name


01:01:37.000 --> 01:01:38.960
is Alex Shipley.


01:01:39.040 --> 01:01:40.087
Shipley.


01:01:41.240 --> 01:01:43.080
He lives in Nashville.


01:01:43.160 --> 01:01:46.800
The man who approached him
was a lawyer out of LA


01:01:46.880 --> 01:01:48.371
named Donald Segretti.


01:01:48.880 --> 01:01:49.881
Segretti.


01:01:52.080 --> 01:01:54.322
Shipley can tell you everything
you need to know.


01:01:54.880 --> 01:01:56.291
<i>Will Shipley talk?</i>


01:01:57.600 --> 01:02:00.126
I guess you're going
to have to find that out.


01:02:00.760 --> 01:02:01.807
One more thing.


01:02:03.640 --> 01:02:06.405
This comes from classified FBI files.


01:02:06.920 --> 01:02:09.730
The Department of Justice has it,
the White House has it,


01:02:11.000 --> 01:02:12.525
and, now, you have it.


01:02:15.240 --> 01:02:18.801
<i>Let's just get on with the election
and stop this nonsense</i>


01:02:18.920 --> 01:02:21.120
<i>about there having been
a political espionage campaign</i>


01:02:21.200 --> 01:02:22.200
<i>against the Democrats.</i>


01:02:22.280 --> 01:02:24.760
<i>Here's what's making the news
at the top of the hour.</i>


01:02:24.840 --> 01:02:28.960
<i>North Vietnamese military attempts
to break through South Vietnamese lines</i>


01:02:29.040 --> 01:02:32.840
<i>have been met with an intense
bombing attack by a US aircraft.</i>


01:02:32.920 --> 01:02:36.480
<i>General Creighton Abrams,
the United States commander in Vietnam,</i>


01:02:36.560 --> 01:02:38.640
<i>ordered every available B-52</i>


01:02:38.720 --> 01:02:40.560
<i>into the northern sector of South Vietnam.</i>


01:02:40.640 --> 01:02:42.440
<i>Though baseball season is over,</i>


01:02:42.520 --> 01:02:45.920
<i>the Philadelphia Phils went to
the Ozarks for a new manager today.</i>


01:02:46.000 --> 01:02:49.083
<i>Los Angeles coach Danny Ozark
was the surprise choice</i>


01:02:49.200 --> 01:02:51.880
<i>of Phils' general manager, Paul Owens.</i>


01:02:51.960 --> 01:02:55.203
<i>Ozark has had no big league
managerial experience...</i>


01:03:39.480 --> 01:03:40.720
Mr. Woodward.


01:03:43.320 --> 01:03:44.685
The story isn't moving.


01:03:45.800 --> 01:03:47.689
Everyone stopped listening to you.


01:03:47.800 --> 01:03:49.404
This isn't the same as before.


01:03:52.760 --> 01:03:54.091
We're lost in detail.


01:03:55.600 --> 01:03:57.204
That's their plan.


01:03:58.200 --> 01:04:00.726
They want everyone confused.


01:04:01.600 --> 01:04:03.443
Confusion is control.


01:04:09.760 --> 01:04:12.684
The truth could ruin the administration.


01:04:15.760 --> 01:04:16.807
How high?


01:04:17.920 --> 01:04:19.251
How high does it go?


01:04:28.240 --> 01:04:30.482
You still don't understand
what I'm giving you.


01:04:34.720 --> 01:04:37.690
This is dangerous stuff you're playing with.


01:04:39.040 --> 01:04:41.725
Especially, if it's known
before November seventh.


01:04:43.280 --> 01:04:45.080
That's election day.


01:04:45.160 --> 01:04:48.050
You put out the right story,
the public will scream.


01:04:49.280 --> 01:04:51.647
The Attorney General
will have to let me keep going.


01:05:14.760 --> 01:05:17.525
My editors know that I'm talking to somebody,


01:05:17.640 --> 01:05:18.880
but not who.


01:05:18.960 --> 01:05:20.200
They don't ask.


01:05:25.520 --> 01:05:28.640
No one understands
how one person knows so much.


01:05:28.720 --> 01:05:31.121
No one can possibly know how much I know.


01:05:34.840 --> 01:05:36.331
With all this mystery,


01:05:37.600 --> 01:05:39.807
there's a nickname for you at the paper.


01:05:42.440 --> 01:05:44.602
- Deep Throat.
- What?


01:05:45.040 --> 01:05:47.008
They didn't know what else to call you.


01:05:48.080 --> 01:05:49.127
That's just...


01:05:50.840 --> 01:05:53.002
They shouldn't have to call me anything.


01:06:02.920 --> 01:06:05.207
Take out your notebook. There's more.


01:06:17.920 --> 01:06:22.080
<i>"FBI agents have established
Watergate bugging incident,</i>


01:06:22.160 --> 01:06:26.085
"massive campaign
of political spying and sabotage.


01:06:26.440 --> 01:06:28.120
<i>"'There is some very powerful information, '</i>


01:06:28.200 --> 01:06:29.960
<i>"said one federal official,</i>


01:06:30.040 --> 01:06:31.400
<i>"'especially if it's known
before election day."'</i>


01:06:31.480 --> 01:06:32.840
<i>The White House
is vigorously denouncing a story</i>


01:06:32.920 --> 01:06:34.320
<i>in</i> The Washington Post <i>this morning</i>


01:06:34.400 --> 01:06:38.007
<i>accusing the administration
of engaging in a secret political war.</i>


01:06:38.160 --> 01:06:41.000
<i>White House Press Secretary Ron Ziegler
is calling the story</i>


01:06:41.080 --> 01:06:43.287
<i>a pack of scurrilous lies and innuendo.</i>


01:06:43.400 --> 01:06:47.200
<i>Based on baseless, cowardly sources
inside the Department of Justice.</i>


01:06:52.720 --> 01:06:54.920
He's here, Mark. He has to be.


01:06:55.000 --> 01:06:56.889
There's a spy in the FBI.


01:06:57.320 --> 01:06:59.320
FBI agents have established,


01:06:59.400 --> 01:07:03.240
one federal investigative official said,
according to FBI reports.


01:07:03.320 --> 01:07:04.811
That's us, god damn it.


01:07:07.160 --> 01:07:11.768
There is information in here
that the bureau only got 72 hours ago.


01:07:11.960 --> 01:07:13.883
Are you goddamn joking?


01:07:15.560 --> 01:07:18.370
Mr. Felt,
you had something you wanted to say.


01:07:23.400 --> 01:07:25.600
The last few days, I've heard various people


01:07:25.680 --> 01:07:28.160
accuse Mr. Lano of leaking to the press.


01:07:28.240 --> 01:07:29.731
- You've got to be kidding me!
- Him?


01:07:30.600 --> 01:07:32.967
And that he and certain newspaper reporters


01:07:33.440 --> 01:07:35.360
- have been seen together.
- I'm going to be sick.


01:07:35.440 --> 01:07:38.285
I wanted to say to you, Mr. Lano,
in front of everyone here


01:07:38.880 --> 01:07:41.884
that I know these are
vicious lies by jealous agents.


01:07:43.920 --> 01:07:46.200
You're doing a fine job, and no matter what,


01:07:46.280 --> 01:07:47.805
the director and I will support you.


01:07:48.680 --> 01:07:50.011
Mr. Gray.


01:07:51.680 --> 01:07:54.684
I may not be an FBI lifer like some of you.


01:07:55.600 --> 01:07:57.523
I'm certainly no Mark Felt.


01:07:58.000 --> 01:08:01.607
Since I arrived here,
I have put up with paranoia,


01:08:01.720 --> 01:08:04.000
insubordination, second-guessing.


01:08:04.080 --> 01:08:06.048
Gentlemen, it's come-to-Jesus time.


01:08:08.000 --> 01:08:12.800
Whoever the leaker is,
whoever is the Judas among you,


01:08:12.880 --> 01:08:16.480
betraying me,
the other good men in this room,


01:08:16.560 --> 01:08:18.120
his family, God,


01:08:18.200 --> 01:08:21.320
not to mention the bureau
and the legacy of J. Edgar Hoover,


01:08:21.400 --> 01:08:22.447
step forward.


01:08:24.400 --> 01:08:27.404
Right here, right now.


01:08:52.160 --> 01:08:56.165
Charlie, we got an office pool
on who the leak is.


01:08:56.960 --> 01:08:58.690
My money's on you.


01:09:19.920 --> 01:09:21.490
It's just one big game, Charlie.


01:09:23.280 --> 01:09:25.726
We're all just chess pieces.
You gotta remember that.


01:09:28.160 --> 01:09:29.969
What's the body count?


01:09:31.040 --> 01:09:32.690
Eight, so far.


01:09:33.160 --> 01:09:36.562
You, me, a few guys on my team.


01:09:39.920 --> 01:09:42.651
- Where are they sending you?
- St. Louis.


01:09:44.840 --> 01:09:46.888
But I don't know
how much more I have left in me.


01:09:48.560 --> 01:09:49.641
You?


01:09:50.680 --> 01:09:51.920
San Francisco.


01:09:53.040 --> 01:09:54.371
Well, at least, it's Frisco.


01:09:55.240 --> 01:09:56.287
Yeah.


01:09:58.600 --> 01:09:59.647
Great.


01:10:01.680 --> 01:10:03.762
How many years you put in here, Charlie?


01:10:11.000 --> 01:10:12.047
The whole run.


01:10:13.320 --> 01:10:14.845
My kids were born here.


01:10:21.480 --> 01:10:23.120
<i>Whatever Watergate was, whatever it wasn't,</i>


01:10:23.200 --> 01:10:26.204
<i>the American people don't seem
to understand, nor care,</i>


01:10:26.440 --> 01:10:29.285
<i>as Nixon has won in a landslide.</i>


01:10:39.720 --> 01:10:41.927
I appreciate you taking the time, Mr. Felt.


01:10:42.560 --> 01:10:45.769
I always take care of my people, Mr. Bates.


01:10:48.280 --> 01:10:50.760
In fact, my father always said to me,


01:10:51.120 --> 01:10:57.162
"Mark, whatever we do,
we have to make our lives vectors."


01:10:57.480 --> 01:11:01.849
Lines with force and direction.


01:11:06.800 --> 01:11:11.920
You have to destroy anything
that is sick beyond repair


01:11:12.000 --> 01:11:15.040
to rescue it from its agony.


01:11:15.120 --> 01:11:16.201
Mark.


01:11:17.360 --> 01:11:18.361
And...


01:11:19.120 --> 01:11:23.125
And the agony it causes everyone else,
Mr. Bates.


01:11:31.880 --> 01:11:35.009
<i>It was thought that he might have
a little bit of difficulty.</i>


01:11:49.440 --> 01:11:51.727
- Mr. Felt.
- What are you doing, Charlie?


01:11:57.280 --> 01:11:59.169
What is it, Mr. Bates?


01:12:11.480 --> 01:12:13.881
Here's to you. Bravo.


01:13:27.600 --> 01:13:29.880
Genesis commune.


01:13:29.960 --> 01:13:31.769
Ben Lomond, California.


01:13:32.400 --> 01:13:33.527
Check it thoroughly.


01:13:56.520 --> 01:13:59.365
These leaks
are driving the White House crazy.


01:14:01.040 --> 01:14:02.883
The White House thinks it knows who it is.


01:14:04.720 --> 01:14:06.131
Your name came up.


01:14:09.560 --> 01:14:15.408
Do you have any idea what that would mean?


01:14:15.760 --> 01:14:17.285
Treason, for one.


01:14:18.000 --> 01:14:21.000
Betrayal of everything
the FBI stands for, for another.


01:14:21.080 --> 01:14:22.844
Everything you stand for.


01:14:23.760 --> 01:14:25.364
So, why would I do it?


01:14:26.120 --> 01:14:27.201
I don't know.


01:14:28.560 --> 01:14:30.528
I can't imagine their thinking.


01:14:33.760 --> 01:14:35.683
Why don't they fire me then?


01:14:36.400 --> 01:14:37.811
You know everything.


01:14:38.840 --> 01:14:42.891
To them, the only thing worse
than keeping you is firing you.


01:14:47.280 --> 01:14:49.010
Dean did say something strange.


01:14:49.440 --> 01:14:52.285
Apparently, they know everything
going on inside our shop.


01:14:52.800 --> 01:14:55.929
- They have a source.
- Inside the FBI?


01:14:56.480 --> 01:15:01.725
He said they hear everything.


01:15:21.640 --> 01:15:24.040
We just swept your office for bugs, Mr. Felt.


01:15:24.120 --> 01:15:25.531
Do it again!


01:15:43.360 --> 01:15:44.646
The knives are out.


01:15:45.600 --> 01:15:47.011
More than you know.


01:15:48.200 --> 01:15:49.327
<i>Am I safe?</i>


01:15:50.160 --> 01:15:51.207
<i>No one is.</i>


01:15:52.200 --> 01:15:55.249
The White House
is gonna sanitize the entire town.


01:15:55.400 --> 01:15:59.000
<i>The director of Central Intelligence
will be gone by morning.</i>


01:15:59.080 --> 01:16:00.200
<i>Why?</i>


01:16:00.280 --> 01:16:03.602
Apparently, he couldn't
smoke you out fast enough.


01:16:05.160 --> 01:16:06.287
The source


01:16:07.720 --> 01:16:09.290
of all those stories.


01:16:11.840 --> 01:16:13.490
Where does the CIA stand?


01:16:14.760 --> 01:16:16.922
<i>The CIA is building a wall.</i>


01:16:18.280 --> 01:16:19.400
<i>We'll stay out of your way,</i>


01:16:19.480 --> 01:16:21.403
but if we're forced to protect ourselves,


01:16:21.880 --> 01:16:22.881
we will.


01:16:24.000 --> 01:16:27.320
<i>The FBI will never reach the CIA on this.</i>


01:16:27.400 --> 01:16:28.686
And the White House?


01:16:29.400 --> 01:16:32.051
Presidents come and go,


01:16:32.160 --> 01:16:33.651
but the CIA stays.


01:16:34.280 --> 01:16:35.645
The FBI stays.


01:16:37.880 --> 01:16:39.371
We are the constants.


01:16:41.080 --> 01:16:42.366
<i>I almost forgot.</i>


01:16:43.720 --> 01:16:47.361
<i>Time</i> magazine's person of the year
is going to be Richard Nixon.


01:16:51.520 --> 01:16:52.806
I thought you'd like to know.


01:16:55.880 --> 01:16:56.927
Happy holidays.


01:17:36.520 --> 01:17:39.285
The president told me
the unthinkable has happened.


01:17:40.160 --> 01:17:41.969
He actually misses Hoover.


01:17:43.200 --> 01:17:45.362
"Hoover would have gotten
the dogs off him," he said.


01:17:46.240 --> 01:17:48.243
"He'd have everyone scared to death."


01:17:57.520 --> 01:18:00.683
The White House is going
to make me director permanently.


01:18:01.800 --> 01:18:03.006
Congratulations.


01:18:07.640 --> 01:18:09.768
Bill Sullivan will be my number two.


01:18:20.920 --> 01:18:22.809
You know what the president said to me today?


01:18:22.920 --> 01:18:26.766
He said, "The Germans had the right idea
during World War ll.


01:18:28.160 --> 01:18:32.040
"If they went through a town and one
of their soldiers got hit by a sniper,


01:18:32.120 --> 01:18:35.488
"they'd line up the whole goddamn town
and kill everyone."


01:18:38.080 --> 01:18:42.165
He said, "It's time to clean out the FBI."


01:18:47.600 --> 01:18:49.640
You know what that will mean for me.


01:18:49.720 --> 01:18:51.324
Remember, they're afraid of you.


01:18:57.920 --> 01:19:00.969
Mark, if you did know something,
you could come to me.


01:19:01.440 --> 01:19:04.091
We'd be able to work it out together.
We could do something about it.


01:19:06.360 --> 01:19:08.249
I can't protect you anymore.


01:19:11.440 --> 01:19:12.965
Just give 'em what they want.


01:19:14.720 --> 01:19:16.563
The traitor's head on a platter.


01:20:05.320 --> 01:20:07.480
So, the president asked me what he should do.


01:20:07.560 --> 01:20:11.281
And, I tell him, get rid of everyone
in the interest of the nation.


01:20:11.880 --> 01:20:13.484
I didn't mean me, of course.


01:20:18.560 --> 01:20:20.403
You don't have many friends left, you know.


01:20:21.280 --> 01:20:24.648
A bunch of your FBI pals
told me to cut your nuts off.


01:20:28.240 --> 01:20:30.322
Think they'll let you keep your badge?


01:20:31.400 --> 01:20:33.243
You got a lot of people worried
in Washington.


01:20:33.800 --> 01:20:35.404
They think you're gonna unwrap everything.


01:20:36.000 --> 01:20:37.650
Everything from all the years.


01:20:38.080 --> 01:20:42.688
Everything we, you and I, know.


01:20:42.960 --> 01:20:44.530
Is that what you want to know, Bill?


01:20:46.120 --> 01:20:48.646
This your last little errand?


01:20:50.760 --> 01:20:52.444
To help the president sleep at night.


01:20:54.560 --> 01:20:56.642
I'm just sayin', you open those scabs,


01:20:58.400 --> 01:20:59.765
a lot of things underneath.


01:21:00.960 --> 01:21:02.610
Just remember, no one likes informers.


01:21:03.640 --> 01:21:05.483
They only remember you as a rat,


01:21:05.800 --> 01:21:09.122
even if you were their...
Even if you were their rat!


01:21:16.320 --> 01:21:19.881
Mr. Felt, Mr. Miller's on the phone.
He needs to speak with you.


01:21:37.920 --> 01:21:40.287
- This is Special Agent Clark.
- I don't want to know his name.


01:21:41.520 --> 01:21:43.284
Tell him what you told Mr. Bates and me.


01:21:44.080 --> 01:21:46.003
I don't think you have anything
to worry about, Mr. Felt.


01:21:47.880 --> 01:21:49.240
You don't think.


01:21:49.320 --> 01:21:50.401
Specific.


01:21:56.520 --> 01:21:59.444
The commune where the subject, Joan Felt...


01:21:59.560 --> 01:22:00.925
Do not say her name.


01:22:06.040 --> 01:22:07.087
Where the target is...


01:22:09.080 --> 01:22:10.923
Definitely some people of interest in there.


01:22:12.960 --> 01:22:15.202
- Maybe some with the Underground.
- But the target?


01:22:18.480 --> 01:22:19.925
If you ask me,


01:22:21.240 --> 01:22:23.368
just someone's kid looking for a way home.


01:22:34.800 --> 01:22:36.960
We never spoke. No paper.


01:22:37.040 --> 01:22:38.201
You don't know anything.


01:23:08.320 --> 01:23:10.050
Do you know your physics, Sandy?


01:23:12.320 --> 01:23:13.845
If you tap repeatedly


01:23:14.760 --> 01:23:17.605
on the post of a building,
and the tapping is relentless,


01:23:20.120 --> 01:23:21.360
it creates a rhythm.


01:23:22.800 --> 01:23:26.240
If you do that long enough
and steadily enough, it will feed back.


01:23:26.320 --> 01:23:28.440
The frequencies will align,


01:23:28.520 --> 01:23:30.480
the molecules will scramble,


01:23:30.560 --> 01:23:35.441
and the whole thing, the whole building
will come apart from the inside


01:23:35.560 --> 01:23:37.164
and collapse in on itself,


01:23:37.280 --> 01:23:39.328
and all come tumbling down.


01:23:40.840 --> 01:23:42.840
The molecules are beginning to scramble.


01:23:42.920 --> 01:23:45.969
The FBI is coming apart.
Do you know where that takes us?


01:23:46.280 --> 01:23:49.440
Do you want a country
this big, this angry, this confused


01:23:49.520 --> 01:23:51.124
without a police department?


01:23:56.440 --> 01:23:57.771
Get out your notebook.


01:24:00.200 --> 01:24:02.840
May, 1969 and February, 1971.


01:24:02.920 --> 01:24:06.607
Mark, are you sure about this?


01:24:06.720 --> 01:24:09.760
Between those dates,
White House employees were wiretapped.


01:24:09.840 --> 01:24:12.685
Many of them aides to the Secretary of State


01:24:12.920 --> 01:24:15.605
and five reporters,
including <i>The New York Times.</i>


01:24:17.080 --> 01:24:18.411
You're kidding.


01:24:22.800 --> 01:24:25.451
- This is hard for you.
- What part?


01:24:27.800 --> 01:24:29.564
All this truth.


01:24:32.120 --> 01:24:34.885
The truth is hard for you.


01:24:42.280 --> 01:24:46.600
The FBI illegally,
unconstitutionally and reprehensibly


01:24:46.680 --> 01:24:49.120
bugged and taped


01:24:49.200 --> 01:24:51.560
and secretly photographed and memorialized


01:24:51.640 --> 01:24:53.802
every move that those people made.


01:24:54.640 --> 01:24:58.042
Them and their wives and
their mistresses and homosexual lovers.


01:25:01.320 --> 01:25:03.163
- Who did the wiretaps?
- Bill Sullivan.


01:25:03.360 --> 01:25:05.761
It became a rogue FBI operation.


01:25:06.360 --> 01:25:09.364
Sullivan drove it. Sullivan and
the White House by themselves.


01:25:11.400 --> 01:25:12.686
How 'bout you?


01:25:14.640 --> 01:25:15.880
What do you know?


01:25:15.960 --> 01:25:20.600
About everything else,
I knew every sordid little detail.


01:25:20.680 --> 01:25:22.011
But not this.


01:25:22.840 --> 01:25:24.444
They knew they couldn't tell me about this.


01:25:25.480 --> 01:25:26.845
Yeah, they couldn't count on you.


01:25:28.400 --> 01:25:32.720
The White House is packing
all its crimes in separate little boxes.


01:25:32.800 --> 01:25:36.122
Watergate, the spying, the ugliness, the rot.


01:25:36.600 --> 01:25:39.560
Each thing in a different box,
so that no one can put it together,


01:25:39.640 --> 01:25:41.920
so that no one sees it's all connected.


01:25:42.000 --> 01:25:45.800
And no one will care.
But it's all the same big thing.


01:25:49.440 --> 01:25:52.489
And Watergate? Just the gateway.


01:25:58.520 --> 01:26:01.171
Can you get the story out
before Gray's confirmation hearing?


01:26:02.600 --> 01:26:03.965
What you're doing


01:26:05.480 --> 01:26:08.006
will bring down the whole house of cards.


01:26:10.680 --> 01:26:13.126
But then, you already knew that.


01:26:17.000 --> 01:26:18.730
<i>Gray is ready to fall now.</i>


01:26:19.240 --> 01:26:20.810
<i>Watch where it leads.</i>


01:26:36.960 --> 01:26:38.803
Any last-minute advice?


01:26:40.960 --> 01:26:42.485
We've gone over everything.


01:26:43.680 --> 01:26:45.284
They'll go easy.


01:26:46.000 --> 01:26:48.003
You're the president's man.


01:26:50.640 --> 01:26:52.882
Mr. Gray. What about this?


01:26:54.640 --> 01:26:56.688
I don't know what my position should be.


01:26:58.280 --> 01:26:59.964
It was before your time.


01:27:01.760 --> 01:27:03.205
Tell the truth.


01:27:04.440 --> 01:27:06.090
No one can argue with the truth.


01:27:08.680 --> 01:27:11.680
Mr. Gray, this <i>Time</i> magazine article
by Sandy Smith


01:27:11.760 --> 01:27:15.640
contains information on alleged wiretaps
requested by the White House


01:27:15.720 --> 01:27:17.480
installed by the FBI.


01:27:17.560 --> 01:27:19.085
How do you respond to these charges?


01:27:20.280 --> 01:27:22.044
It was before my time, Senator.


01:27:24.960 --> 01:27:27.611
What about the assertion in this article


01:27:27.840 --> 01:27:31.080
that a White House aide
slipped Donald Segretti,


01:27:31.160 --> 01:27:34.000
a target of the bureau's
Watergate investigation,


01:27:34.080 --> 01:27:36.003
copies of what the FBI had?


01:27:36.600 --> 01:27:37.920
We didn't look into that.


01:27:38.000 --> 01:27:40.321
- Why on Earth not?
- I'll have to look into that.


01:27:40.440 --> 01:27:43.330
Did you know that the White House
had your confidential file?


01:27:45.360 --> 01:27:46.964
I did. Yes, Senator.


01:27:56.560 --> 01:27:58.440
Let me tell you how that might have happened.


01:27:58.520 --> 01:27:59.920
Please do.


01:28:00.000 --> 01:28:02.320
White House counsel John Dean told me


01:28:02.400 --> 01:28:06.320
the White House wanted everything
the FBI had on Watergate


01:28:06.400 --> 01:28:08.482
to help with its own investigation.


01:28:09.440 --> 01:28:11.682
Mr. Dean took all those FBI files.


01:28:11.800 --> 01:28:14.531
How many Bureau reports are we talking about?


01:28:14.760 --> 01:28:17.809
How many reports did you give Mr. Dean?


01:28:18.760 --> 01:28:20.364
I believe it was 82.


01:28:21.320 --> 01:28:25.610
As the acting director of the FBI,
why on Earth would you do that?


01:28:25.760 --> 01:28:28.000
- Because I was told to.
- By who?


01:28:28.080 --> 01:28:29.730
Who would have ordered that?


01:28:36.920 --> 01:28:38.285
The president.


01:28:41.720 --> 01:28:44.960
<i>One of the most difficult decisions
of my presidency,</i>


01:28:45.040 --> 01:28:46.600
<i>I accepted the resignations</i>


01:28:46.680 --> 01:28:50.000
<i>of two of my closest associates
in the White House,</i>


01:28:50.080 --> 01:28:52.720
<i>Bob Haldeman and John Ehrlichman.</i>


01:28:52.800 --> 01:28:57.602
<i>The counsel to the president, John Dean,
has also resigned.</i>


01:28:58.040 --> 01:29:00.280
<i>The nation tonight is in the midst
of what may be</i>


01:29:00.360 --> 01:29:04.000
<i>the most critical constitutional crisis
in its history.</i>


01:29:04.080 --> 01:29:08.483
<i>As a result of the president's action,
the Attorney General has resigned.</i>


01:29:09.720 --> 01:29:13.042
<i>L. Patrick Gray,
head of the FBI for nearly a year,</i>


01:29:13.160 --> 01:29:17.080
<i>will now never take the chair
occupied by J. Edgar Hoover.</i>


01:29:17.160 --> 01:29:19.120
<i>John Dean told me, during a conversation,</i>


01:29:19.200 --> 01:29:21.320
<i>that the White House masterminded a cover-up.</i>


01:29:21.400 --> 01:29:22.845
<i>I began by telling the president</i>


01:29:22.960 --> 01:29:25.240
<i>that there was a cancer growing
on the presidency,</i>


01:29:25.320 --> 01:29:28.360
<i>that it was important this cancer
be removed immediately</i>


01:29:28.440 --> 01:29:30.920
<i>because it was growing more deadly every day.</i>


01:29:40.600 --> 01:29:41.931
I found Joan.


01:29:43.120 --> 01:29:44.645
Let's go get her.


01:30:00.960 --> 01:30:03.611
My God. It's my parents.


01:30:13.720 --> 01:30:15.688
It's all right. I know.


01:30:24.280 --> 01:30:25.645
Mark?


01:30:36.240 --> 01:30:37.651
Dad.


01:30:53.680 --> 01:30:55.045
This is your grandson.


01:30:58.280 --> 01:31:00.169
Come here, sweetheart.


01:31:00.800 --> 01:31:01.801
There we go.


01:31:15.760 --> 01:31:17.524
I had this feeling when I was little,


01:31:21.480 --> 01:31:23.084
that I couldn't see into his eyes,


01:31:28.640 --> 01:31:30.085
that he didn't approve of me.


01:31:33.800 --> 01:31:38.169
That he was holding me up
to some impossible standard.


01:31:42.680 --> 01:31:43.920
That was me.


01:31:49.080 --> 01:31:50.760
When you were sick and you were little,


01:31:50.840 --> 01:31:52.968
it was your father
who climbed into bed with you


01:31:53.920 --> 01:31:55.445
in his shoes,


01:31:56.640 --> 01:31:58.131
his holster, his suit.


01:32:00.960 --> 01:32:05.045
He'd sit with you for hours
and rock you till you fell back asleep.


01:32:58.160 --> 01:33:01.005
Look at that big baby.


01:33:12.760 --> 01:33:13.807
Thank you.


01:33:16.880 --> 01:33:19.326
- Mr. Director? We're ready.
- Mr. Felt.


01:33:26.000 --> 01:33:27.684
- Mark.
- Mr. Ruckelshaus.


01:33:31.720 --> 01:33:33.006
Thank you.


01:33:34.160 --> 01:33:37.240
Mr. Felt, thank you for 31 years of service


01:33:37.320 --> 01:33:39.129
to the Federal Bureau of Investigation.


01:33:39.720 --> 01:33:41.370
- Thank you.
- Hear, hear!


01:33:51.360 --> 01:33:52.600
Congratulations.


01:34:26.480 --> 01:34:28.483
- Hey, congratulations.
- Good luck, Mark.


01:34:28.600 --> 01:34:29.806
Well done, Mark.


01:34:33.080 --> 01:34:34.200
Congratulations, sir.


01:34:34.280 --> 01:34:36.601
<i>I have never been a quitter.</i>


01:34:37.200 --> 01:34:39.800
To leave office before my term is completed


01:34:39.880 --> 01:34:42.611
is abhorrent to every instinct in my body.


01:34:44.800 --> 01:34:46.245
<i>But as president,</i>


01:34:46.600 --> 01:34:49.729
<i>I must put the interests of America first.</i>


01:34:56.600 --> 01:34:57.647
<i>Therefore,</i>


01:34:58.800 --> 01:35:02.407
I shall resign the presidency
effective at noon tomorrow.


01:35:03.360 --> 01:35:07.445
<i>Vice President Ford,
will be sworn in as president</i>


01:35:07.760 --> 01:35:10.445
<i>at that hour, in this office.</i>


01:35:20.400 --> 01:35:22.520
Counterespionage expert.


01:35:22.600 --> 01:35:23.761
Nazi hunter.


01:35:25.520 --> 01:35:27.966
You, Mr. Felt, are the G-man's G-man,


01:35:28.920 --> 01:35:30.126
a hero and a patriot,


01:35:31.240 --> 01:35:33.083
and we are a grateful nation.


01:35:34.320 --> 01:35:37.369
Ladies and gentlemen, for the past few weeks


01:35:37.480 --> 01:35:40.360
you've heard through testimony
the sounds of the bombs


01:35:40.440 --> 01:35:43.840
of the PLO and the Weather Underground
ringing in your ears.


01:35:43.920 --> 01:35:45.560
People died.


01:35:45.640 --> 01:35:48.291
We were a nation at war at home and abroad.


01:35:49.120 --> 01:35:50.485
We don't dispute that.


01:35:51.440 --> 01:35:54.250
Now, we ask you to listen
for the sound of the Constitution.


01:35:56.680 --> 01:35:57.727
You hear that?


01:35:59.200 --> 01:36:01.248
It doesn't make quite as much noise
as a bomb, does it?


01:36:02.920 --> 01:36:05.800
It just sits there, silent,
like our conscience,


01:36:05.880 --> 01:36:09.601
just as it's done for the last 200 years.


01:36:10.320 --> 01:36:11.560
Mr. Felt.


01:36:13.160 --> 01:36:14.969
On September eighth, 1972,


01:36:15.080 --> 01:36:19.080
did you order 143 FBI agents
across the country


01:36:19.160 --> 01:36:20.680
to break into the homes of relatives


01:36:20.760 --> 01:36:22.720
of alleged members
of the Weather Underground,


01:36:22.800 --> 01:36:24.723
to wiretap their phones and bug their homes?


01:36:24.840 --> 01:36:26.490
- Yes.
- Who else?


01:36:26.800 --> 01:36:27.840
Who else what?


01:36:27.920 --> 01:36:29.968
Who else participated in giving those orders?


01:36:33.320 --> 01:36:36.120
- Assistant Director Edward Miller?
- I gave the order.


01:36:36.200 --> 01:36:38.800
Acting Director L. Patrick Gray the third?


01:36:38.880 --> 01:36:40.484
I gave the order.


01:36:40.960 --> 01:36:41.961
Charles Bates?


01:36:47.440 --> 01:36:49.124
You're really gonna sit there and do that?


01:36:50.800 --> 01:36:53.531
You're really gonna take that on
for everybody?


01:36:54.640 --> 01:36:55.971
I gave the order.


01:36:56.840 --> 01:36:59.440
Mr. Felt, you stated that you


01:36:59.520 --> 01:37:01.920
frequently briefed
the Nixon White House on the case.


01:37:02.000 --> 01:37:06.210
Maybe you could just give us
a quick snapshot on how that all worked.


01:37:07.360 --> 01:37:11.763
I was in constant contact
with the White House on many matters.


01:37:14.440 --> 01:37:17.125
In fact, I was in the Oval Office so often,


01:37:18.120 --> 01:37:21.169
people used to say I had to be Deep Throat.


01:37:28.000 --> 01:37:29.684
What did you just say?


01:37:30.000 --> 01:37:34.360
I said I was with the White House,
Dean and so forth, so often,


01:37:34.440 --> 01:37:38.650
people thought I was <i>The Washington</i>
<i>Post's</i> source for Watergate.


01:37:38.960 --> 01:37:41.008
The person they called, "Deep Throat."


01:37:49.640 --> 01:37:51.324
Before the witness is excused,


01:37:53.160 --> 01:37:54.810
are there any questions from the jury?


01:37:58.400 --> 01:38:00.289
Well, were you?


01:38:01.440 --> 01:38:05.127
- Was I what?
- Were you Deep Throat?
